---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Dark Matter Cosmic Web Cheat Sheet | Free Filaments, Voids, Large-Scale Structure"
  description="Complete dark matter cosmic web cheat sheet with filaments, voids, and large-scale structure. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Matter Cosmic Web<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Filaments, voids, and large-scale structure. From dark matter halos to cosmic filaments.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cosmic Web Structure</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Components</h3>
        <pre><code>Filaments: thread-like structures
Walls: sheet-like structures
Voids: empty regions
Nodes: cluster intersections
Scale: 10-100 Mpc</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dark Matter Distribution</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>N-body Simulations</h3>
        <pre><code>Millennium, Illustris, EAGLE
Cold dark matter predicts cosmic web
Bottom-up structure formation
Filaments connect nodes (clusters)
Voids contain few galaxies</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Observational Evidence</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Surveys</h3>
        <pre><code>Sdss, 2dF, DESI, Euclid
Redshift space distortions
Galaaxy clustering statistics
Baryon acoustic oscillations
Weak lensing shear maps</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dark Matter Filaments</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Connect galaxy clusters
Dark matter dominated
Gas temperature: 10⁵-10⁷ K
X-ray emission from hot gas
Gravitational lensing detected</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
